\name{g.part5_analyseSegment_ExtFunType}
\alias{g.part5_analyseSegment_ExtFunType}
\title{Analyse External Function Type Classifications in GGIR Part 5}
\description{
Calculates summary metrics for epoch-by-epoch categorical classifications
generated by external functions with \code{reporttype = "type"} in GGIR Part 5.

For each classification type, the function calculates time spent in the
type, time spent outside defined bouts (unbt), time spent in defined bouts, total
time, mean acceleration, number of blocks, and number of bouts. Metrics are
calculated separately for sleep period time (SPT) and daytime.

External function type classifications are represented internally as the
number of seconds in each epoch assigned to each classification. Bout
definitions are represented by the corresponding binary matrices generated
during the type bout detection step.
}
\usage{
g.part5_analyseSegment_ExtFunType(ts, sse, TOLEVELS, TLEVELS, Tnames, myfun,
                                  ws3new, dsummary, ds_names, si, fi)}
\arguments{
\item{ts}{
Data frame containing the Part 5 epoch-level time series, including
acceleration, day/SPT indicators, and external function type
information.
}
\item{sse}{
Integer vector containing the indices of the epochs belonging to the
current segment.
}
\item{TOLEVELS}{
Matrix containing the number of seconds in each epoch assigned to each
external function type. Columns represent classification types and rows
represent epochs.
}
\item{TLEVELS}{
List containing the binary bout masks for each external function type.
Each element contains one row per bout-duration definition and one column
per epoch.
}
\item{Tnames}{
Character vector containing the names corresponding to the type bout
definitions in \code{TLEVELS}.
}
\item{myfun}{
List defining the external function. The function uses the
\code{colnames} element to identify the external classification variable.
}
\item{ws3new}{
Numeric value specifying the epoch duration in seconds.
}
\item{dsummary}{
Matrix containing the Part 5 summary results. The function adds the
external function type metrics to this matrix.
}
\item{ds_names}{
Character vector containing the names of the Part 5 summary variables.
The function appends the names of the external function type metrics.
}
\item{si}{
Integer identifying the current row of \code{dsummary} to which the
results are written.
}
\item{fi}{
Integer identifying the current output column position in
\code{dsummary} and \code{ds_names}.
}
}
\value{
A list containing:
\describe{
\item{\code{dsummary}}{
The updated Part 5 summary matrix containing the external function type
metrics.
}
\item{\code{ds_names}}{
The updated vector of summary variable names.
}
\item{\code{fi}}{
The updated output column index.
}
}
\details{
For each external function type, metrics are calculated separately for SPT
and daytime.

The following metrics are generated:

\itemize{
\item Time spent outside any defined bout (\code{unbt}).
\item Time spent in each defined bout-duration category.
\item Total time spent in the classification type.
\item Mean acceleration during epochs classified as the type.
\item Number of blocks, defined as contiguous periods in which the type is
present.
\item Number of bouts for each defined bout-duration category.
}

A block is based on the original epoch-level type classification and is
therefore independent of the bout-duration criteria. Bout counts and bout
durations are based on the bout masks stored in \code{TLEVELS}.

The function is intended to be called internally by
\code{g.part5_analyseSegment} and is not normally called directly by users.
}
